Added `process=compare` to load two run artifacts and compute run-to-run distance metrics (JS/KL for r/theta, KS/Wasserstein for size, polar density L1/L2, NN KS), writing `compare_summary.json`, `compare_table.csv`, and a histogram overlay plot with sanitized input metadata; wired new compare config defaults, process registration, a self-consistency test, and documented the process in the catalog.
- Metrics implementation and outputs live in `src/synthlab/processes/compare.py`, and the process is registered in `src/synthlab/processes/__init__.py`.
- Default compare config (fixed bins, smoothing epsilon, NN sampling cap) is in `conf/compare/default.yaml` and loaded via `conf/process/compare.yaml`.
- Self-consistency test for near-zero distances is in `tests/test_T0204_compare_distance_metrics.py`.
- Process catalog updated in `docs/10_PROCESS_CATALOG.md`.

